  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Enhancing Ethiopia&#xbf;s Readiness for the Implementation of the AfCFTA Digital Trade Protocol</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The project&apos;s general objective is to support Ethiopia&#xbf;s readiness and promotes the implementation of the AfCFTA Digital Trade Protocol through improved regulatory alignment, the development of digital infrastructure, and inclusive engagement with stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Specific Objectives are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf; SO1: To align Ethiopia&#xbf;s digital trade regulatory and policy frameworks with the provisions of the AfCFTA DTP, by supporting policy reviews and alignment, harmonization of relevant laws (e.g. on e-commerce, data protection, cybersecurity), and the development of a coherent national implementation roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf; SO2: To strengthen Ethiopia&#xbf;s digital trade infrastructure and systems interoperability, notably through the piloting of digital payment platforms (e.g. PAPSS integration), the enhancement of e-commerce systems, and the promotion of paperless trade tools that facilitate seamless cross-border transactions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf; SO3: To build institutional and stakeholder capacity and promote inclusive participation in digital trade implementation, through targeted training programs, multi-stakeholder dialogues, and awareness-raising programs aimed at government institutions, SMEs, women and youth entrepreneurs, and other key actors in the digital economy.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
